          "unit_id": "airport_travel",
          "title": "Flight to Dublin",
          "description": "Entiende avisos y normas del aeropuerto con la voz pasiva. Y el future continuous: This time tomorrow we'll be flying.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "airport_checkin",
              "title": "The passive",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Flight to Dublin",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "We've made it! Just in the nick of time."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "Good morning. Passports, please. Are you checking in any bags?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Yes, one suitcase."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "Your bag will be sent directly to Dublin. Did you pack it yourself?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Yes, I did."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "I'm afraid it's too heavy. Bags over twenty-three kilos are charged an extra fee."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "How much is it?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "Thirty pounds. Your boarding passes have been sent to your phones. Boarding will begin at gate seven at ten forty."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Agent",
                        "text": "Attention, please. Flight EI six five three to Dublin has been delayed by thirty minutes. Passengers are asked to wait in the departure lounge."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Delayed? After all that running!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Never mind. I'm really looking forward to showing you Dublin."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "And I'm looking forward to meeting your mam. I'm a bit nervous, too!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Don't be. She's been asking about you since Christmas."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "April, Easter holidays. Lucía got the senior job, and she and Daniel are flying to Dublin to celebrate. But they set off late, and the traffic to the airport is terrible."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"Your bag will be sent directly to Dublin.\" Who sends it?",
                        "options": [
                          "It isn't important (the airline)",
                          "Lucía"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"Bags over twenty-three kilos are charged an extra fee.\" The structure is…",
                        "options": [
                          "be + past participle",
                          "have + past participle"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"The flight has been delayed.\" Which tense is it?",
                        "options": [
                          "present perfect passive",
                          "past simple passive"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"They set off late.\" Set off means…",
                        "options": [
                          "salir, ponerse en camino",
                          "apagar"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "The passive",
                    "explanation": "La pasiva (be + participio) pone el foco en la acción o en lo que la recibe, no en quién la hace. Es muy habitual en avisos, normas y noticias: The flight has been delayed. Passengers are asked to wait.\n\nEl verbo be cambia de tiempo y el participio no: is charged, was built, has been delayed, will be sent.\n\nSi queremos decir quién hace la acción, usamos by: The airport was designed by a famous architect.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Tiempo",
                        "Activa",
                        "Pasiva"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Presente",
                          "They charge a fee.",
                          "A fee is charged."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pasado",
                          "They built the airport in 1957.",
                          "The airport was built in 1957."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Present perfect",
                          "They have delayed the flight.",
                          "The flight has been delayed."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Futuro",
                          "They will send your bag.",
                          "Your bag will be sent."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Your bag will be sent directly to Dublin.",
                      "Bags over twenty-three kilos are charged an extra fee.",
                      "Your boarding passes have been sent to your phones.",
                      "Passengers are asked to wait in the departure lounge."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Future continuous: will be + -ing",
                    "explanation": "El future continuous (will be + -ing) describe una acción que estará en marcha en un momento del futuro: This time tomorrow we'll be walking around Dublin (mañana a esta hora estaremos paseando por Dublín).\n\nTambién se usa para planes que van a pasar en el curso normal de las cosas, y para preguntar por planes con educación: Will you be using the car tonight? (¿vas a usar el coche esta noche?).\n\nNegativa: won't be + -ing: I won't be working on Friday.\n\nCompáralo con will + verbo, que es una acción puntual: The plane will land at twelve. At twelve we'll be landing (en pleno aterrizaje).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "En marcha en el futuro",
                          "At eleven we'll be flying over the Irish Sea."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "I won't be working at Easter."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta educada",
                          "Will you be checking in any bags?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Acción puntual (will)",
                          "The flight will leave at ten forty."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "This time tomorrow we'll be walking along the River Liffey.",
                      "Don't call me at eleven. I'll be flying to Dublin.",
                      "Will you be needing a taxi at the airport?",
                      "Maureen will be waiting for us at the station."
                    ]
                  }
                },
